# API Development Guide

## Endpoint Structure

```typescript
// All endpoints follow this pattern
export async function handler(req: Request) {
  // 1. Validate input with Zod schema
  // 2. Check authentication/authorization
  // 3. Perform business logic
  // 4. Return standardized response
}
```

## Response Format

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": { },
  "meta": { "requestId": "..." }
}
```

## Error Handling

Use AppError class from /src/lib/errors

# Examples

## Example 1: Basic Usage

**Input:**
```
Create a user registration endpoint
```

**Output:**
```typescript
export async function registerUser(req: Request) {
  const body = await req.json();
  const validated = UserSchema.parse(body);

  const user = await db.users.create({
    email: validated.email,
    passwordHash: await hash(validated.password)
  });

  return Response.json({ success: true, userId: user.id });
}
```

## Example 2: With Validation Error

**Input:**
```
Handle invalid email in registration
```

**Output:**
```typescript
// Zod will throw, caught by error boundary
if (!validated.email.includes('@')) {
  throw new ValidationError('Invalid email format');
}
```

# Component Examples

## Basic Button Component

**Request:** Create a primary button

**Generated:**
```tsx
interface ButtonProps {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  onClick?: () => void;
  disabled?: boolean;
}

export function Button({ children, onClick, disabled }: ButtonProps) {
  return (
    <button
      className="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded hover:bg-blue-700 disabled:opacity-50"
      onClick={onClick}
      disabled={disabled}
    >
      {children}
    </button>
  );
}
```

## Form Input with Label

**Request:** Create an email input field

**Generated:**
```tsx
export function EmailInput({ value, onChange, error }: EmailInputProps) {
  return (
    <div className="space-y-1">
      <label className="text-sm font-medium">Email</label>
      <input
        type="email"
        value={value}
        onChange={(e) => onChange(e.target.value)}
        className={`w-full p-2 border rounded ${error ? 'border-red-500' : ''}`}
      />
      {error && <p className="text-red-500 text-sm">{error}</p>}
    </div>
  );
}
```

